  "passage": {
    "text": "In our view, the latest supply-and-demand data are consistent with recent pressure on gold prices. As we previously noted, sustained investmentdemand and robust central bank purchases are essential for gold prices to remain above USD 4,000/oz. And here the focus, particularly for investment demand, remains on US monetary policy and the direction of US interest rates. With the market still pricing Fed rate hikes this year, price risks remain skewed to the downside in the near term, leaving room for gold to pull back toward USD 3,850/oz. However, we do not believe investors should become too negative on the metal either, especially over the next 12 months.",
